From: rime-fork <rime-fork@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:09:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Rebrand=20as=20Sable=20(=E8=B2=82=E6=AF=AB),=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?the=20Penglai=20front=20end?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sable is Penglai's own macOS front end built from Squirrel. It must be able
to run next to Squirrel without either one picking up the other's input
source, IMK connection or distributed notifications, so every outward
identifier changes while Swift type and file names stay the same (fewer
conflicts when syncing with upstream).

- Bundle id im.penglai.inputmethod.Sable, product/executable/module Sable,
  version 0.1.0. Info.plist uses $(EXECUTABLE_NAME), $(PRODUCT_NAME) and
  $(PRODUCT_MODULE_NAME): with the product renamed, a literal "Squirrel"
  executable or Squirrel.SquirrelInputController class would keep the input
  method from starting.
- One input mode, im.penglai.inputmethod.Sable.Hant (primary .hant), shown
  as 貂毫 in the input menu.
- The status-item and stranded-composition checks compare against
  Bundle.main.bundleIdentifier instead of a hard-coded prefix.
- Register the running bundle (Bundle.main.bundleURL) instead of
  /Library/Input Methods/Squirrel.app: Sable installs per user in
  ~/Library/Input Methods.
- Distributed notifications, IMK connection, librime distribution
  (Sable / 貂毫 / rime.sable), log directory and launch-crash record all
  use Sable names, so `Squirrel --reload` no longer reaches Sable.
- Remove Sparkle: the official appcast only ships Squirrel. Drops the
  updater, the "Check for updates" menu item, the feed keys and the
  framework from the build phases.
- Icons: Sable.icon (app) and resources/penglai.pdf (menu bar), copied in
  from rime-penglai's branding/ by build.sh.

The front-end config is still squirrel.yaml here; renaming it to
sable.yaml is a separate patch.
